   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.1. Increased institutional capacity of employer and business membership organizations (EBMOs)</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2022-23, the Federation of Egyptian Industries (FEI) introduced numerous new and enhanced services in various areas, including human resources; gender; employer-led childcare; child labour; human trafficking; refugees and host communities; and corporate social responsibility. 

One significant addition to FEI&#x2019;s services was the introduction of an internship day in March 2023, aimed at improving labour market matching for its member enterprises and creating opportunities for young people. This new service complemented FEI&#x2019;s existing apprenticeship and job placement services for refugees and host communities. This allowed FEI to interact with new target groups and demonstrate its commitment to social value by integrating youth from host communities and refugees into the labour market. During the internship day, 1200 youth and 40 companies participated. This event together with the other job placement services resulted in the signing of 145 employment contracts of one-year duration in FEI member companies.

FEI also improved its existing training service on HR and Gender Academy by publishing standardised learner and trainer guides. In Feb 2022, FEI conducted a training of trainers for the Academy based on the new guides.  Subsequently, FEI conducted two new cycles of its two-weeks long HR and Gender Academy (March 2022 &amp; March 2023) attracting over 130 fee-paying human resources managers and personnel from over 65 companies. Despite the introduction fees, the Academy remained highly attractive ensuring the sustainability of the service. In March 2022, the HR and Gender Academy was held in Aswan, marking the first time it was conducted outside the capital. This expansion allowed FEI to broaden its service offering and visibility in regions of the country where its presence was less prominent. The ILO, with the support of donor partnership from Finland, the Netherlands, Norway, the US, the UK, and Sweden, supported the Federation of Egyptian Industries (FEI) to strengthen its position and visibility and promoting its social agenda through the provision of technical support in the domains of human resources, gender, refugees and host communities. In particular, the ILO supported FEI in conceptualising the internship day and partnered with FEI to give the event high visibility. The ILO also provided technical inputs in the organisation of the training of trainers in March 2022, offered technical inputs to the drafting and publication of the learner and trainer guides for the HR and Gender Academy, co-organized the HR and Gender Academy and facilitated several sessions in the two cycles of the HR and Gender Academy that were implemented in during the biennium. The ILO also conducted knowledge needs assessment on child labour and supported FEI to develop new contents in its training and advisory services on child labour, employer-led childcare, child labour, human trafficking, freedom of association and corporate social responsibility. The support included the co-organisation of workshops, the publication of guidance notes, standard operating procedures.</narrative>
   </description>
