  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 6.2. Increased capacity of Member States to strengthen policies and strategies to promote and ensure equal opportunities, participation and treatment between women and men, including equal remuneration for work of equal value</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Ministry of Labour, led by its Gender Unit adopted and launch, the National Action Plan on Gender Equality and Non-discrimination at Work (NAP) in April 2022 under the auspices of the Egyptian Prime Minister. The Action Plan aims at fostering a gender-responsive labour environment in 6 key working areas:
 1) legislation;
 2)  empowerment and participation rate;
 3) protection and equality; 
4) knowledge infrastructure; 
5) awareness and community support; 
6) governance and participation.
The NAP is currently used as the core national document on gender equality at work to define detailed actions to take towards fully achieving that objective.
  The ILO, supported the Ministry of Labour to design and draft its first National Action Plan on Gender Equality and Non-discrimination at Work (NAP) for Egypt.
From October 2021 to February 2022, the ILO convened regular meetings of the Steering Committee to discuss various aspects of the challenges related to achieving gender equality in the world of work, the current situation of gender equality at work (based on the result of a desk review process which was developed with ILO&#x2019;s assistance), related development interventions,  the elements that should be included in the various components of the NAP, including identification of specific stakeholders along with their roles and responsibilities during its implementation, mains recommendations for achieving gender equality in the world of work, etc.
In March 2022, the ILO organized a NAP validation workshop, to present the draft of the NAP, and to gather  inputs in order to finalize the action plan.</narrative>
   </description>
